## USGS dataRetrieval Elements

Comparing what fields (elements) are returned with `dataRetrieval::readWQPdata` `dataProfile` calls (see `readWQPdata` help for options for both Legacy and WQX3).



```{r, echo=FALSE, message=FALSE, warning=FALSE}
library(remotes)
library(devtools)
load_all()

library(tidyverse)
library(readr)
library(knitr)

library(dataRetrieval) # v2.7.18.9002
# Old version of dataRetrieval (temporary)
#remotes::install_github("DOI-USGS/dataRetrieval", ref = "develop", dependencies = TRUE, force = TRUE)
# to update EPATADA package to use this version of the package

```



## Example readWQPdata query

USGS site (USGS-440504121435800). Note as of 5/13/2025 the beta version of WQP was only returning USGS data, not WQX data. The Portal team are aware and working on it. Will query data and return different profiles types (e.g., 'resultPhysChem' vs 'fullPhysChem')



```{r}
#| echo: false
#| message: false
WQPquery2 <- list(siteid = "USGS-440504121435800"#, #Middle Green Lake (1980-1981)   McKenzie River at Springfield ("USGS-440508122581200")
                  #startDate = "1975-01-01",
                  #endDate = "1978-12-31",
                  #characteristicName = "Temperature, water"

)

################
# COMPARE OUTPUT FROM resultPhysChem and fullPhysChem
# LEGACY PORTAL data call (note: 'resultPhysChem' ONLY works with LEGACY)
result.basic <- dataRetrieval::readWQPdata(WQPquery2,
                                           service = "Result", # beta "ResultWQX3"
                                           dataProfile = "resultPhysChem", #"fullPhysChem",
                                           ignore_attributes = T)

# BETA PORTAL data call (note different service and dataProfile) (n = 183 fields vs n = 141 with legacy fullPhysChem)
result.full <- dataRetrieval::readWQPdata(WQPquery2,
                                          service = "ResultWQX3", # beta "ResultWQX3"
                                          dataProfile = "fullPhysChem", #"resultPhysChem", #"fullPhysChem",
                                          ignore_attributes = T)
# Make column headings a vector
basic <- as.data.frame(colnames(result.basic)) |> 
  rename("basic" = 1) |> 
  mutate(WqxV2.FieldName = basic)

full <- as.data.frame(colnames(result.full)) |> 
  rename("full" = 1) |> 
  mutate(FieldName3.0 = full)

#knitr::kable(basic)
#knitr::kable(full)
```



## Join Legacy and Beta field elements using crosswalk table

Read in WQX crosswalk table to join the basic (legacy) and full (beta) field elements together to compare. Had to modify the crosswalk table to replace special characters in the legacy column (WqxV2.FieldName) so that they will match fields returned in dataRetrieval. For example, 'ActivityStartTime/Time' in crosswalk table vs 'ActivityStartTime.Time' from dataRetrieval.



```{r}
#| echo: false
#| message: false
## Updated crosswalk table (temporary)
## 4/3/25
wqxcrswlk <- readr::read_csv("C:/Users/efergus/OneDrive - Environmental Protection Agency (EPA)/a_WDIB/TADA/WQP_transition/Crosswalk_tables/Temp_Crswlk/wqxcrswlk_temp.csv")
# Need to create additional key fields so that they don't get 'overwritten'
# Need to rename field names to have "." instead of "/"
cols_wqx2 <- wqxcrswlk$WqxV2.FieldName

wqxcrswlk_mod <- wqxcrswlk |> 
  mutate(WqxV2.FieldName = str_replace_all(WqxV2.FieldName, c('/' = '\\.')))|> 
  mutate(wqx3 = FieldName3.0,
         wqx2 = WqxV2.FieldName)


# Full Join the basic table to the crosswalk table - will return all x rows followed by unmatched y rows (this is true for basic legacy profile e.g., 'LastUpdated' is not in the crosswalk table)
basic_mod <- wqxcrswlk_mod |> 
  full_join(basic, join_by(WqxV2.FieldName)) 

# Full join full table to modified crosswalk table
all_mod <- basic_mod |> 
  full_join(full, join_by(FieldName3.0)) |> 
  select(wqx3, wqx2, basic, full)

# Filter fields returned with readWqpdata profiles (from 409 to 223)
# https://stackoverflow.com/questions/33520854/filtering-data-frame-based-on-na-on-multiple-columns/69395357
all_red <- all_mod |> 
  filter_at(vars(basic,full), any_vars(!is.na(.))) 

# WRITE MODIFIED TABLE
write_csv(all_red, "C:/Users/efergus/OneDrive - Environmental Protection Agency (EPA)/a_WDIB/TADA/WQP_transition/dataRetrieval_output/result.dr.full.basic.profile.csv")

```



## Fields not returned in the beta data profile call
Fields from the legacy (readWQPdata - 'resultPhysChem' profile) that may not have an exact match with fields returned in the beta (readWQPdata - 'fullPhysChem' profile). Note - we may need to update the crosswalk table to catch some of these that have equivalent beta versions but may not have been mapped properly. 


```{r}
#| echo: false

basic_only <- all_red |> 
  filter(is.na(full))

knitr::kable(basic_only)


```



## Fields in beta (full) but not in basic (legacy)
Fields in the beta ('fullPhysChem' profile) that may not have a legacy match in the crosswalk table because there wre one-to-many matches (as noted by 'see Comment field'. Or beta fields that are missing from the crosswalk table in general. 


```{r}
#| echo: false
full_only <- all_red |> 
  filter(is.na(basic)) |> 
  filter(wqx2 == "see Comment field"|
           is.na(wqx3))

knitr::kable(full_only)
```



## Fields that may need to be updated in the crosswalk table
wqx fields represent the crosswalk table and DR fields represent the dataRetrieval output


```{r}
#| echo: false

fix <- data.frame(
  wqx3 = c("Result_DetectionCondition",NA, NA, "ResultBiological_GroupSummaryWeightMeasure","ResultBiological_GroupSummaryWeightMeasureUnit","SampleCollectionMethod_Description"),
  wqx2 = c("ResultDetectionConditionText",NA, NA,"GroupSummaryCountWeight/MeasureValue", "GroupSummaryCountWeight/MeasureUnitCode","see_Comment"),
  DR3 = c("Result_ResultDetectionCondition", "Activity_StartDateTime","Activity_StartTimeZone_offset","GroupSummaryWeight_Measure","GroupSummaryWeight_MeasureUnit","SampleCollectionMethod_Description"),
  DR2 = c("ResultDetectionConditionText","ActivityStartDateTime","ActivityStartTime.TimeZoneCode_offset",NA, NA,"SampleCollectionMethod.MethodDescriptionText")
    
)

knitr::kable(fix)
```

